"title": "Glossary",
"text": "Project Hub ERC's project management reporting tool, replacing PWA. PWA Project Web App — the previous tool, retired on 30 September. Plan The record for one project in Project Hub, with all its tabs. Project ID The reference Project Hub gives a project when it's first saved (e.g. PRJ-1044). Used at the start of every risk and issue name. Record Owner Who owns the plan record. You to begin with; your Teams group once it's linked. Planner Microsoft Planner, which runs the Tasks tab. Parent task / subtask A phase (parent) and the pieces of work inside it (subtasks). Critical milestone A zero-duration task marking an important point. Used in the Power BI reports to show progress. Bucket A column for grouping tasks in Board view. RAG Red / Amber / Green. Risk RAG is worked out from the risk's Likelihood and Impact. 4×4 matrix The risk assessment grid: Likelihood and Impact, each scored one to four stars. Flow An automated action in the command bar — e.g. Escalate Risk to Issue. Get to Green The action you must give when any health rating is Off Track — how you'll bring it back. 3-month look-ahead The three Narrative questions in a status update: expected, achieved, planned. Replaces the Flash Report. Highlight Report The one-page report for each project, on the Status Report tab. Project Lifecycle The five-stage bar at the top of the plan: Initiation, Planning, Delivery, Monitoring & Controlling, Closure. Deactivate The final step of closing a project, which makes the plan read-only. PMO Project Management Office. PID Project Initiation Document — must be saved in the project's documents."
